WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Meet Raahi, a simpler way to complete India’s road services. Sign in with the fictional test account.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:20.000
See the services that matter: licences, vehicles, challans, appointments, documents, PUC and permits.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:30.000
RoadReady plans one successful visit. Describe the goal in everyday language and it detects connected services.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:40.000
It places renewal, address update and challan clearance in the right order, reducing forms and possible visits.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:50.000
Before travel, preflight checks fictional documents and finds a name mismatch that could cause rejection.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:59.000
Resolve it immediately and receive a QR One-Visit Pass without exposing document numbers.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:09.000
Raahi was built with React, TypeScript, Codex and a test-first workflow.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:19.000
The design addresses unclear service boundaries, failed scrutiny, repeated entry, payment uncertainty and vague status.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:29.000
RoadReady combines once-only data, verified digital credentials and document preflight.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:39.000
Working journeys include new licences, renewals, eChallan, RTO comparison, appointments, maps and tracking.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:49.000
All identities, documents, fees, payments, government responses and integrations are fictional.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:55.000
Raahi changes the success metric from forms submitted to citizen work completed.
